A26. Water cutters. ~ BOWS
A28. These turn sheepish after a while. ~ LAMBS
A30. By. ~ AT
A31. You need a low one to legislate. ~ BROW
A33. Shrdluetaoinvxuwpi. ~ PI
A35. This generally comes with a few hops. ~ MALT
A36. An old rake. ~ ROUE
A37. The remains of remains. ~ HASH
A39. Certainly. ~ YES
A40. Dire need. ~ WANT
A41. Ford now leaves the making of this to the soup manufacturers. ~ CAN
A42. A dumpy Greek god with a string to pull. ~ EROS
A44. This, at least, is an attempt. ~ TRY
A45. What every gangster expects to be, every day. ~ SHOT
A47. What a fisherman called a golfer. ~ LIAR
A49. A communist picnic. ~ RIOT
A51. Have being. ~ AM
A52. Men are pelting women with these now. ~ FURS
A53. This here guy. ~ HE
